Directory: FISSION
File:      superheavy_saddles_Bf_WMM.readme (24 May 2026)
*********************************************************

                  SUPERHEAVY_SADDLES_BF_WMM.DAT
    Saddle-point properties and static fission barrier heights
                   of isotopes with Z=98-126
  (Provided by P. Jachimowicz, M. Kowal, J. Skalski, 24 May 2026)
 *****************************************************************

Contents
--------
The file contains saddle-point properties and corresponding static fission barrier heights
calculated using the Warsaw macroscopic-microscopic (WMM) model [1]. It provides saddle-point masses,
total energies, macroscopic and microscopic energy contributions, saddle-point deformation parameters,
and static fission barrier heights corresponding to the primary (highest) saddle encountered along the fission path.
The dataset covers 1305 heavy and superheavy nuclei with proton numbers Z=98-126 and neutron numbers N=134-192.
For a given Z, the minimum neutron number increases incrementally with Z. A search for saddle-points was performed
using the "imaginary water flow" method in three consecutive stages. The search was carried out within a deformation
space defined by a standard spherical-harmonic expansion of the nuclear surface. Five- (for nonaxial shapes)
and seven-dimensional (for reflection-asymmetric shapes) deformation spaces were used. Further details of the model
and computational procedure can be found in Ref. [1].

Format
------
Each record of the file contains

     Z      : proton (charge) number
     N      : neutron number
     A      : mass number
     M      : saddle-point mass excess [MeV]
     Etot   : total saddle-point energy [MeV]
     Emac   : macroscopic saddle-point energy [MeV]
     Emic   : microscopic saddle-point energy [MeV]
     b2-b8  : saddle-point deformation parameters
     Bf     : static fission barrier height [MeV]

The corresponding Fortran format specification is (3i4,15f8.2).

References
----------
[1] P. Jachimowicz, M. Kowal, J. Skalski, At. Data Nucl. Data Tables 138, 101393 (2021).
